n never have too many main course recipes, so give Mexican Chicken & Rice Bowl a try. This recipe serves 4 and costs $4.1 per serving. One serving contains <b>839 calories<\\/b>, <b>62g of protein<\\/b>, and <b>37g of fat<\\/b>. This recipe is liked by 1 foodies and cooks. Only a few people really liked this Mexican dish. From preparation to the plate, this recipe takes approximately <b>30 minutes<\\/b>. It is a good option if you\'re following a <b>gluten free and dairy free<\\/b> diet. This recipe from Foodista requires limes, salsa, olive oil, and black beans. All things considered, we decided this recipe <b>deserves a spoonacular score of 88%<\\/b>. This score is great. <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/spoonacular.com\\/recipes\\/mexican-chicken-rice-bowl-1584583\\\">Mexican Chicken & Rice Bowl<\\/a>, <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/spoonacular.com\\/recipes\\/cha-cha-bowl-for-mexican-chicken-and-black-bean-rice-bowl-soraya-darabi-and-alexa-andrzejewski-50-women-game-changers-in-food-473926\\\">Cha Cha Bowl ( for Mexican Chicken and Black Bean Rice Bowl)- Soraya Darabi and Alexan Andrzejewski \\u2013 50 Women Game Changers In Food<\\/a>, and <a href=\\\"https:\\/\\/spoonacular.com\\/recipes\\/chicken-brown-rice-bowl-zinques-le-bowl-1561757\\\">Chicken Brown Rice Bowl (Zinque\'s Le Bowl)<\\/a> are very similar to this recipe.\",\"cuisines\":[\"Mexican\"],\"dishTypes\":[\"lunch\",\"main course\",\"main dish\",\"dinner\"],\"diets\":[\"gluten free\",\"dairy free\"],\"occasions\":[],\"instructions\":\"<ol><li>Place the thinly sliced chicken in a bowl. Drizzle with enough olive oil to coat. Sprinkle with salt, pepper and a nice amount of fresh chopped parsley. Let sit for 20 minutes.<\\/li><li>Fire up the grill and cook the chicken for about 4 minutes per side, depending on the thickness. Set aside.<\\/li><li>Dice the avocado and toss with lime juice to coat and sprinkle with a little salt.<\\/li><li>Cook the brown rice according to package instructions.<\\/li><li>To build the bowls, 